{% extends "_layout.html.j2" %}
{% set active = 'audit' %}
{% set canonical_path = "/product/audit" %}
{% set page_description = "A complete diagnostic of your AI visibility in minutes. 5 engines × 40 buyer queries = 200 answers, scored for visibility and citations. From $29." %}
{% block title %}Audit — AI visibility diagnostic | monitoraeo{% endblock %}

{% block schema %}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Service",
  "@id": "{{ _base_url }}/product/audit#service",
  "name": "monitoraeo AI visibility audit",
  "serviceType": "AI answer engine visibility audit",
  "provider": { "@id": "{{ _base_url }}/#org" },
  "areaServed": "Worldwide",
  "description": "{{ page_description }}",
  "url": "{{ _canonical }}",
  "offers": [
    {
      "@type": "Offer",
      "name": "Two Engine Audit",
      "price": "29",
      "priceCurrency": "USD",
      "url": "{{ _base_url }}/pricing",
      "description": "Google AI Overviews + ChatGPT, 40 buyer queries × 2 engines = 80 AI answers, hallucination + accuracy scoring, prioritised action plan."
    },
    {
      "@type": "Offer",
      "name": "Full Audit",
      "price": "79",
      "priceCurrency": "USD",
      "url": "{{ _base_url }}/pricing",
      "description": "All 5 engines (Google AI Overviews, ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, Gemini), 40 queries × 5 engines = 200 AI answers, engine heatmap, per-engine sentiment + accuracy scoring, prioritised action plan."
    }
  ]
}
</script>
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is an AEO audit?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "An AEO (Answer Engine Optimisation) audit measures how often Claude, ChatGPT, Perplexity, Gemini and Google AI Overviews name a brand, cite its domain, and recommend it in buyer-facing answers. monitoraeo runs 40 buyer questions across all 5 engines (200 AI answers), scores visibility, citation rate, sentiment and hallucination risk per engine, and produces a prioritised action plan."}
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Which AI engines does monitoraeo test?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Five engines: Google AI Overviews (free preview tier and up), ChatGPT (Two Engine Audit and up), Claude, Perplexity and Gemini (Full Audit only). Each engine is queried with the same buyer questions and uses its native web search."}
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How long does an audit take?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Free preview: ~30 seconds (8 questions on Google AI Overviews only). Full paid audit: 5–10 minutes (40 questions × 5 engines = 200 individual answers). The report lands in your dashboard when the run finishes."}
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What's the difference between Two Engine Audit and Full Audit?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Two Engine Audit ($29 one-off) covers Google AI Overviews + ChatGPT — the two engines most buyers actually use. Full Audit ($79 one-off) adds Claude, Perplexity and Gemini for complete coverage. Both tiers include the full hallucination + accuracy scoring and a Claude-generated prioritised action plan."}
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is the free preview really free?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. No card, no signup. The preview runs 8 buyer questions on Google AI Overviews and shows visibility + citation rate. Paid tiers expand the engine set, query count, scoring depth and add the prioritised action plan."}
    }
  ]
}
</script>
{% endblock %}

{% block extra_css %}
  .feature { padding: 24px; border-radius: 22px; background: white; border: 1px solid var(--line); box-shadow: var(--shadow-soft); }
  .feature h3 { margin-top: 0; }
  .feature p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; margin-bottom: 0; }
  .icon-box { width: 44px; height: 44px; border-radius: 14px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--blue), var(--purple)); display: grid; place-items: center; color: white; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 900; margin-bottom: 12px; }
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<span class="eyebrow">Product · Audit</span>
<h1 class="page-title">A complete diagnostic of your AI visibility, in minutes.</h1>
<p class="page-lede">Two layers, one report. <strong>AEO measurement</strong> tests how Claude, ChatGPT, Perplexity, Gemini and Google's AI Overview describe, cite and recommend you across 40 buyer questions. <strong>GEO foundations</strong> inspects your site directly with 15 technical checks — robots.txt, schema, llms.txt, server rendering and more. <a href="/what-is-geo" style="color:var(--blue); font-weight:700;">Why GEO matters →</a></p>

<div style="display:flex; gap:14px; margin-bottom: 28px; flex-wrap:wrap;">
  <a href="/#preview" class="btn-primary">Start with a free preview →</a>
  <a href="/pricing" class="btn-secondary">See pricing</a>
</div>

<h2>What's inside every audit</h2>
<div class="grid-3">
  <div class="feature">
    <div class="icon-box">🧱</div>
    <h3>GEO foundations check</h3>
    <p>15 technical checks on your site itself: robots.txt for AI bots, sitemap, llms.txt, schema.org markup, server-rendered content, metadata, performance. <a href="/what-is-geo" style="color:var(--blue); font-weight:700;">Learn more →</a></p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature">
    <div class="icon-box">📊</div>
    <h3>Visibility &amp; citation scoring</h3>
    <p>For every (engine × query) we measure whether your brand was named in the answer text and whether your domain was cited as a source.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature">
    <div class="icon-box">🌡</div>
    <h3>Engine heatmap</h3>
    <p>Visibility % broken down by engine and query type. See where you're strong (probably brand questions) and where you're missing (usually category and comparison).</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature">
    <div class="icon-box">🥇</div>
    <h3>Competitor share-of-voice</h3>
    <p>Which rivals AI engines name in the same answers — and how often. The brands you compete with for the AI's attention.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature">
    <div class="icon-box">🔗</div>
    <h3>Top-cited source map</h3>
    <p>The 20 domains AI engines pulled from when answering questions in your category. This is your PR target list — get mentioned on these and you'll start getting cited too.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature">
    <div class="icon-box">⚠</div>
    <h3>Hallucination flags</h3>
    <p>A second-pass LLM checks every answer against your business's ground-truth facts and flags any unsupported claims for you to correct.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature">
    <div class="icon-box">📂</div>
    <h3>Per-query drill-down</h3>
    <p>The raw evidence — every AI answer side-by-side, with sentiment tags, citation lists and competitor mentions. The brief your content team needs.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature">
    <div class="icon-box">✅</div>
    <h3>Prioritised action plan</h3>
    <p>Every paid audit ends with a Claude-generated checklist of what to fix first — split into content, schema and entity fixes. Each item explains why it matters, the expected impact and a concrete next step.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<h2>What an audit covers</h2>
<div class="panel">
  <div class="grid-2" style="gap: 20px;">
    <div>
      <h3 style="margin-top:0;">5 AI engines</h3>
      <ul class="bullets">
        <li>Google AI Overviews (via SERP scraping)</li>
        <li>ChatGPT (GPT-5-mini with native web search)</li>
        <li>Claude (Haiku 4.5 with native web search)</li>
        <li>Perplexity (Sonar)</li>
        <li>Gemini (2.5 Flash with grounding)</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 style="margin-top:0;">40 buyer-facing queries</h3>
      <ul class="bullets">
        <li><strong>Brand:</strong> "What is X?", "Is X legit?", "X reviews"</li>
        <li><strong>Category:</strong> "Best [thing] in [region]"</li>
        <li><strong>Problem:</strong> "How do I solve [pain] with…"</li>
        <li><strong>Comparison:</strong> "X vs Y", "Best alternative to Z"</li>
        <li><strong>Vertical:</strong> "[Thing] for [industry]"</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<h2>Audit pricing</h2>
<p>Two one-off audit tiers, plus a free 8-question preview if you want to try it first. Every paid tier includes the prioritised action plan.</p>
<div class="grid-2" style="gap:18px; margin: 14px 0;">
  <div class="feature">
    <div class="icon-box">2×</div>
    <h3>Two Engine Audit — $29 one-off</h3>
    <p style="color:var(--ink-2);">Google AI Overviews + ChatGPT. 40 buyer-facing queries × 2 engines = 80 AI answers. Includes hallucination + accuracy scoring and a Claude-generated prioritised action plan. Best if you want a fast, focused check on the two engines most buyers actually use today.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature">
    <div class="icon-box">5×</div>
    <h3>Full Audit — $79 one-off</h3>
    <p style="color:var(--ink-2);">All 5 engines: Google AI Overviews, ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity and Gemini. 40 queries × 5 engines = 200 AI answers, engine heatmap, per-engine sentiment + accuracy scoring, and the full prioritised action plan. Best if you want complete coverage in a single report.</p>
  </div>
</div>
<div style="margin: 12px 0;">
  <a href="/pricing" class="btn-primary">See full pricing comparison →</a>
</div>

<h2>What you'll know after one audit</h2>
<ul class="bullets">
  <li>Whether AI engines are <strong>recommending you</strong> when buyers in your category ask high-intent questions.</li>
  <li>Which <strong>specific competitors</strong> are being named in your absence — and on which engines.</li>
  <li>Which <strong>publications, review sites and reference domains</strong> AI engines treat as authoritative — your earned-mention target list.</li>
  <li>Whether AI engines are <strong>making false claims</strong> about your business that you need to correct in source content.</li>
  <li>The <strong>specific gaps</strong> by query type (brand vs category vs comparison) so you know where to point your content team.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Looking for ongoing tracking?</h2>
<p>An audit is a snapshot. AI engines drift weekly — answers change, new competitors enter, citations shuffle. The <a href="/product/monitoring" style="color:var(--blue); font-weight:700;">Monitoring product</a> re-runs your audit every month, charts the trend, and alerts you when visibility moves. Want the background on what we're measuring? <a href="/what-is-aeo" style="color:var(--blue); font-weight:700;">Read: What is AEO?</a></p>

